                            <note>Written by the same hand as <ref target="coloph1"/> (<ref target="#h2"/>). According to 
                                <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/ZABJTC9I"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Triulzi2006Orality"/><title level="a">When orality turns to writing: two documents from Wälläga, Ethiopia</title><title level="j">Journal of African Cultural Studies</title><author><forename>Alessandro</forename><surname>Triulzi</surname></author><publisher>Routledge</publisher><date>2006</date><biblScope unit="volume">18</biblScope><biblScope unit="chapter">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43–55</biblScope><note type="accessed">2026-03-27</note><note type="url">https://www.jstor.org/stable/25473355?seq=1</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Triulzi2006Orality</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Triulzi2006Orality</note><citedRange unit="page">51</citedRange></bibl>, this section was 
                                added by <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4938HabtaMa"><roleName type="title">Daǧǧāč</roleName> Habtamāryām</persName> 
                                to his father’s genealogical record in <ref target="#ms_i1.1"/>, contrary to <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/N6HPGQK3"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/><title level="m">Catalogue des manuscrits éthiopiens de l’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei: Fonds Conti Rossini et Fonds Caetani 209, 375, 376, 377, 378</title><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><pubPlace>Roma</pubPlace><publisher>Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei</publisher><date>1976</date><series><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note><citedRange unit="page">144</citedRange></bibl>, who hypothesized based on notes by 
                                <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS3182ContiRo">Carlo Conti Rossini</persName> that <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4938HabtaMa">Daǧǧāč Habtamāryām</persName> 
                                and <persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS4222Gabraeg">Daǧǧāč Gabra ʾƎgziʾabǝḥer</persName> were one and the same person.
                                According to <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/N6HPGQK3"><seg type="book"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue"/><title level="m">Catalogue des manuscrits éthiopiens de l’Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei: Fonds Conti Rossini et Fonds Caetani 209, 375, 376, 377, 378</title><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><author><forename>Stefan</forename><surname>Strelcyn</surname></author><pubPlace>Roma</pubPlace><publisher>Accademia Nazionale dei Lincei</publisher><date>1976</date><series><title level="s">Indici e Sussidi Bibliografici della Biblioteca</title><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope></series><biblScope unit="volume">9</biblScope><note type="tags"><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note></note><note type="tag">Cataloguing</note><note type="tag">Ethiopic</note><note type="tag">bm:IHABook182</note><note type="tag">bm:Strelcyn1976Catalogue</note><citedRange unit="page">145</citedRange></bibl>,
                                comprising only three pages on <locus from="39r" to="40r"/>, but according to 
                                <bibl corresp="http://zotero.org/groups/358366/items/ZABJTC9I"><seg type="journalArticle"><!-- attributes from original bibl--></seg><ptr target="bm:Triulzi2006Orality"/><title level="a">When orality turns to writing: two documents from Wälläga, Ethiopia</title><title level="j">Journal of African Cultural Studies</title><author><forename>Alessandro</forename><surname>Triulzi</surname></author><publisher>Routledge</publisher><date>2006</date><biblScope unit="volume">18</biblScope><biblScope unit="chapter">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">43–55</biblScope><note type="accessed">2026-03-27</note><note type="url">https://www.jstor.org/stable/25473355?seq=1</note><note type="tags"><note type="tag">bm:Triulzi2006Orality</note></note><note type="tag">bm:Triulzi2006Orality</note><citedRange unit="page"/></bibl>, written on 
                                <locus from="37" to="40"/>.</note>
